====================================================================================================
v119  ATTACKING G:  qubit-wise vs general commuting
====================================================================================================
  V6's cost IS G. nisq_v6 hardcodes qubit_wise=True, the most restrictive
  grouping. General commuting is strictly coarser - any abelian Pauli set is
  simultaneously diagonalisable by a Clifford.
  TIER C for the counts (structural, sanctioned); tier A for depth.

====================================================================================================
PART 1  THE FAMILIES WHERE G IS ALREADY SMALL
====================================================================================================
  If G is 1 or 3 there is nothing to win, and that is most of what NISQ
  hardware targets. Confirming it, so the scope line is measured not assumed.

    problem              terms    G(qwc)   G(general)   ratio
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   Heisenberg N=4           9        3          2       1.50x
   Heisenberg N=6          15        3          2       1.50x
   Heisenberg N=8          21        3          2       1.50x
   MaxCut N=6              11        1          1       1.00x
   H2                       5        2          2       1.00x
   LiH                     15        3          2       1.50x

====================================================================================================
PART 2  JORDAN-WIGNER ELECTRONIC STRUCTURE - where G ~ N^4.24
====================================================================================================
  v30's generator, so these G(qwc) should reproduce v30's column.

     N   terms   G(qwc)   G(general)   ratio    T/G(qwc)  T/G(gen)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
      6     171       75          17     4.41x       2.28     10.06
      8     652      259          54     4.80x       2.52     12.07
     10    1825      656         133     4.93x       2.78     13.72
     12    4170     1420         227     6.26x       2.94     18.37

   fitted   T ~ N^4.61     G(qwc) ~ N^4.24     G(general) ~ N^3.79
   v30 measured G(qwc) ~ N^4.24 - this should reproduce it.

====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
   THE EXPONENT IS WHAT MATTERS, not the ratio at any single N.

     fitted   G(qwc) ~ N^4.24     G(general) ~ N^3.79     gap 0.45

   A PARTIAL REDUCTION - about half a power. V6's cost, which IS G, falls
   from N^4.24 to N^3.79. Whether that survives the Clifford depth it
   costs is the next question, and it is not answered here.

   IT DOES NOT WIDEN V6's ADVANTAGE, and that is easy to state wrongly.
   C_PS/C_V6 = 2MG/G = 2M, so G CANCELS and a smaller G helps parameter-shift
   by exactly the same factor. At N=12 the picture is

                        qwc          general
      V6                1420    ->     227
      parameter-shift  2M*1420  ->  2M*227 
      ratio               2M            2M      unchanged

   So this lowers the FLOOR for both rather than changing the gap. Worth
   having because V6's remaining quantum cost IS G - but it sits in the same
   bucket as double factorization, not stacked on top of it.

   SANITY: v30 measured G(qwc) ~ N^4.24 on this same generator. If the fitted
   G(qwc) above is far from that, the comparison is against the wrong
   Hamiltonian and nothing here is meaningful.

   WHAT IS NOT PAID FOR HERE. A general-commuting group needs a Clifford to
   diagonalise it; a qubit-wise group needs only the single-qubit H and
   Sdg-H that _basis() already emits. So any reduction below is bought with
   basis-rotation depth, on the axis V6 already loses. Measuring that cost
   requires synthesising the diagonalising Clifford per group, which is the
   build this file deliberately stops short of - the exponent decides
   whether it is worth doing at all.

   Scope: one JW term-generator (v30's), coefficients ignored since neither
   grouping depends on them, four sizes, no circuits built.
